WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.679
A custom ride is yours alone, so it stops whenever you do: pause, lose the bike,

00:00:07.679 --> 00:00:08.808
leave or end.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.182
Pause holds the clock, the plan and the readouts at six fifty-two. The resistance

00:00:15.182 --> 00:00:18.720
stays in your hands, and Resume carries on from there.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.074
If the bike stops answering, the ride pauses on its own and says so. Reconnect, and

00:00:28.074 --> 00:00:30.301
it waits for you to press Resume.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.776
Open the ride with no bike, and it waits at zero behind Connect your bike. With

00:00:40.776 --> 00:00:43.838
Bluetooth off, it asks you to turn it on first.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:54.520
Library pauses the ride and asks: save it and open the library, discard it, or keep

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.670
riding. Escape keeps riding.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:07.219
End saves the ride and opens Profile, and so does the plan's end. A ride under a

00:01:07.219 --> 00:01:10.157
minute is not kept, and Profile says so.

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:17.628
Leave this ride, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.774
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.631
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:34.631 --> 00:01:36.302
every hill and interval.

00:01:36.647 --> 00:01:41.825
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:41.825 --> 00:01:47.273
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.263
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:53.101
A custom workout lives under Profile.
